# Pin these bundled content assets to LF so SHA-256 integrity gates
# (QuranImportService, AzkarImportService, TalbiyahRepository,
# PilgrimageDuaRepository) never silently break on a Windows checkout.
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true rewrites plain LF text assets to
# CRLF on clone/checkout, changing their bytes and permanently failing
# verification (import refused, feature shows an empty/stuck state)
# even though the committed content is correct — the bug is in the
# checkout, not the data.
#
# NOT applied to assets/quran/tanzil-quran-data.xml: that file's
# canonical committed content has some pre-existing CRLF line endings
# by original upstream design, and forcing eol=lf on it would rewrite
# those and break its own hash gate. That file already round-trips
# correctly under core.autocrlf, so it's deliberately left alone here.
assets/quran/tanzil-uthmani.txt text eol=lf
assets/quran_translations/*.txt text eol=lf
assets/azkar/*.json text eol=lf
assets/talbiyah/*.json text eol=lf
assets/pilgrimage/*.json text eol=lf
